### Member Registration API — the three calls Descope's flow connectors make.
### Run the API in Development (Facets stub + the dev connector key) and send these in order.

@host = https://localhost:7001
@connectorKey = dev-connector-key
@email = jane.member@example.com

### Phase 2 — Descope has verified the email; create the pending member record.
# Copy `userId` from the response into @userId below.
POST {{host}}/api/initiateRegistration
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "firstName": "Jane",
  "lastName": "Member",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-04-23",
  "zipCode": "12345"
}

### ^ paste the returned userId here
@userId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Phase 3 — store the password (hashed; Descope never sees it).
POST {{host}}/api/registration/password
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "userId": "{{userId}}",
  "password": "Str0ng!Pass",
  "confirmPassword": "Str0ng!Pass"
}

### Phase 4 — confirm eligibility and create the user.
POST {{host}}/api/completeRegistration
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "ssn": "123-45-6789",
  "memberId": null
}

### Phase 4, unhappy path — the stub treats an SSN ending 0000 as "no such member".
POST {{host}}/api/completeRegistration
Content-Type: application/json
X-Connector-Key: {{connectorKey}}

{
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "ssn": "123-45-0000"
}

### No connector key — expect 401.
POST {{host}}/api/initiateRegistration
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nokey@example.com",
  "firstName": "No",
  "lastName": "Key",
  "dateOfBirth": "1985-04-23",
  "zipCode": "12345"
}

### Health
GET {{host}}/health
